# 19-10-leg1-fix-verify.console — the -s '' fix verified LIVE (2026-11-15)
#
# The owner's first Leg-1 attempt parked on an empty "Plan 9 console"
# window (no rio, no password prompt): the wrapper exec'd drawterm
# without -s '', so the secstore probe defaulted to the authserver and
# the 3-part auth address passed through netmkaddr AS-IS — the probe
# dialed the AUTH port and mutual-parked against authsrv's
# readn(TICKREQLEN).  The 19-08 gate carries -s '' (its line 314 form);
# the wrapper now does too.
#
# Venue: linux-x86_64, KVM (q35, slirp + the committed D-04 hostfwd
# pair), a fresh `nix run .#boot-r9-x64 -- --system=cpu` guest whose
# cpurc ladder ran PAIR-OK -> ETHER-OK -> KEYFS-OK -> AUTHSRV-LISTEN
# -> FACTOTUM-OK -> LISTEN-17010 -> DONE before any dial.  r9 pin
# df4ad78 (flake.lock); drawterm = packages.x86_64-linux.drawterm
# (zffcffb4jsvagwf98sa5vbqp87753zms-drawterm-19.06).  Driver: expect
# on a pty (a throwaway /tmp script — the two passes below are its
# complete captured output).  No password was ever sent: the fix pass
# is killed AT the prompt (the auth handshake surface is the
# verification bar); no credential material appears in this capture.
#
# PASS A — the OLD form (the package binary directly, no -s ''), the
# owner's reported shape; 25s park window:
#
--- pass A: old form (no -s '') ---
spawn /nix/store/zffcffb4jsvagwf98sa5vbqp87753zms-drawterm-19.06/bin/drawterm -G -O cpu=127.0.0.1,auth=tcp!127.0.0.1!5670,user=glenda

VERDICT-OLD: PARKED — no password prompt in 25s (the owner-reported defect REPRODUCED: the secstore probe mutual-parks on the AUTH port)
#
# PASS B — the FIXED wrapper (`nix run .#drawterm`, DISPLAY unset ->
# the loud -G fallback); the flake evaluated the DIRTY working tree,
# so the run exercised the edited wrapper text itself:
#
--- pass B: the fixed wrapper ---
spawn nix run .#drawterm
